<div class="container mt-5 bg-subtle-secondary">
    <h3 class="border-bottom pb-1">How it works</h3>
    <ol class="list-unstyled vstack gap-3 fs-">
        <li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
            <i class="bi bi-1-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
            <div class="vstack">
                <strong>Load a directory.</strong>
                <span
                    >Select a local directory from your computer and it will
                    automatically load all images inside it.</span
                >
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
            <i class="bi bi-2-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
            <div class="vstack">
                <strong>Label the images.</strong>
                <span
                    >The images will appear one by one and in alphabetical order
                    by file name. Just type the label that you want to set for
                    that image and click save. The tool will automatically
                    advance to the next image. If you make a mistake or don't
                    want to label the image shown yet, you can use the
                    «previous» and «next» buttons.</span
                >
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hstack align-items-start gap-3">
            <i class="bi bi-3-circle mt-1 fs-5"></i>
            <div class="vstack">
                <strong>Export the results.</strong>
                <span
                    >One you've finished labeling all images, click the export
                    button and you will be prompted to save a text (.txt) file.
                    This file will contain one row per labeled image with the
                    format
                    <code>image-name.abc&lt;tab&gt;label&lt;lf&gt;</code>.</span
                >
            </div>
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>
